@0    = ~So, <CHARNAME>, where did you learn your fighting skills? From what I have seen you have the skills of a seasoned warrior.~
@1    = ~I was taught basic fighting skills at Candlekeep and learn more as I traveled along the Sword Coast fighting bandits and other enemies.~
@2    = ~It's not really any of your business, Callisto. Leave me be.~
@3    = ~I am self taught actually. I learned much as I traveled along the Sword Coast fight bandits and other people with the intent to do me harm.~
@4    = ~So you learned something from that place full of peaceful monks? Amazing!~
@5    = ~Why is it amazing? They were good tutors in armed and unarmed combat. I learned a lot from them.~
@6    = ~They did teach me a few things, but I learned mostly as I adventured along the Sword Coast.~
@7    = ~I have seen you in combat, <CHARNAME>, your fierceness in battle does not strike me as something learned by a bunch of pacifistic monks.~
@8    = ~Well I did and its not that big of a deal. Since we are on the topic of training, where did you learn yours from?~
@9    = ~Not sociable today aye? So be it, I will say nothing more!~
@10   = ~For being self taught, you have done well for yourself. If you had proper training you could have better.~
@11   = ~Proper training? I don't think I need it, I have done pretty good so far.~
@12   = ~Yeah, yeah, I am not a perfect killing machine like you. Just leave me alone!~
@13   = ~Training? Perhaps you could show me a few moves.~
@14   = ~Oh really? If you say so, <CHARNAME>.~
@15   = ~Since we are on the topic of training, where did you learn yours from?~
@16   = ~Me? Show you? Heh that's a good one, <CHARNAME>. I am not one for training.~
@17   = ~Well it didn't hurt to ask. Since we are on the topic of training, where did you learn your fighting skills from?~
@18   = ~Me? Where did I learn to fight? I had many "tutors" who taught me in my early years. My first one was a ruthless warlord named Medurr. He taught me the finer points in sword fighting and the ability to inflict maximum pain on your target before they died in agony. Ah yes, he was good at what he did.~
@19   = ~Medurr sounds like an interesting teacher. Who were your other tutors?~
@20   = ~I was also trained by Taeh, who taught me how to channel my emotions and use them effectively in combat. She taught me how to use my rage and anger in combat. She was a harsh task master, she would use a barbed whip on me if I screwed up. I have many scars on my body thanks to her.~
@21   = ~She sounds like quite the sadist. Whatever happen to your teachers?~
@22   = ~Medurr knew first hand what a painful death was when his pupil became his better and showed him that paybacks were a bitch. Taeh was hamstrung and whipped to death when I showed her what rage was all about.~
@23   = ~You killed your own teachers? Why?~
@24   = ~I could not allow them to instruct others in their fighting skills, only I could have their knowledge.~
@25   = ~Medurr's demise was more personal. That bastard would force himself on me when I slept. This went on for years until the day came when I showed him a whole new meaning of what it meant to be forcefully penetrated.~
@26   = ~I relished in his death, it was liberating. Enough down memory lane, let's go.~
@27   = ~So, <CHARNAME>, where did you learn your fighting skills? From what I have seen you need some practice.~
@28   = ~I am self taught actually. I learned much as I travelled along the Sword Coast fight bandits and other people with the intent to do me harm.~
@29   = ~Not socialable today aye? So be it, I will say nothing more!~
@30   = ~Oh really? If you say so <CHARNAME>.~
@31   = ~Me? Show you? Heh that's a good one <CHARNAME>. I am not one for traing.~
@32   = ~Well it didn't hurt to ask. Since we are on the topic of training, where did you learn yours from?~
@33   = ~I was also trained by Taeh, who taught me how to channel my emotions and use them effectivly in combat. She taught me how to use my rage and anger in combat. She was a harsh task master, she would use a barbed whip on me if I screwed up. I have many scars on my body thanks to her.~
@34   = ~<CHARNAME> you've been quiet lately, why is that?~
@35   = ~I've been wondering why you destroyed Belmin's village.~
@36   = ~I'm appalled we killed Belmin to protect you. I think you should leave.~
@37   = ~Is it true you were responsible for Belmin's village being destroyed or were you just goading him into a fight?~
@38   = ~Why do you ask? Well, let me tell you why, <CHARNAME>, if you really, really must know! Their third in command, Shalinteer, lived there. They refused to give him up, so my army laid waste to the village.~
@39   = ~That sounds extreme, killing all of those people just to get Shalinteer.~
@40   = ~That's horrible! I don't think we need you any more. You should leave, Callisto.~
@41   = ~Extreme? No I think not. They were told to surrender him and we would have left them in peace. But they foolishly decided to protect him, which by doing so they became my enemy.~
@42   = ~I think you heard enough on this for now, <CHARNAME>, perhaps more later.~
@43   = ~Even though I love a good fight, I was not looking for one that day.~
@44   = ~My army attacked his village. Their third in command, Shalinteer, lived there. They refused to give him up, so my army laid waste to the village.~
@45   = ~Leave? I think you should reconsider that fool. Yes, yes I really think you should.~
@46   = ~I said for you to leave. Don't come back unless you want a fight.~
@47   = ~Sorry I wasn't thinking straight. A lot on my mind. One of those things that's on my mind is why did you attack Belmin's village?~
@48   = ~(Callisto looks at you coldly, than a wicked smile crosses her face.) Ha ha ha!! Why wait?~
@49   = ~<CHARNAME> you've been quiet lately, why is that hmmm?~
@50   = ~I was thrilled we killed Belmin to protect you. A day is not complete without spilling blood.~
@51   = ~That sounds extreme, killing all of those people just to get Shalinteer. I would have done the same thing if it was me.~
@52   = ~It is good to hear we have something in common. Perhaps I will indulge you more later on this.~
@53   = ~(Callisto smiles at you.) I believe we will get along wonderfully. Ah yes, yes. Perhaps I will tell you more about my past later on.~
@54   = ~Why do you keep looking at me dwarf?~
@55   = ~Fer a bloody long legged elf I find you attractive. Why don't we get to know each other better?~
@56   = ~Ha! ha! I did not know dwarves could tell jokes. You and me? If I thought you were serious I would bleed you nice and slow.~
@57   = ~Har! Me kind of women! Full of fire and spite. We would get along just fine aye. Why not show me how talented you are with that knife?~
@58   = ~Keep it up little one and I'll make sure you are short in "other" areas of the body.~
@59   = ~Heh a man's has to try no? But don't ye fret girly, ye are me one and only. I'll git to ye yet.~
@60   = ~Well don't count on it. The chances of that happening is one in a billion.~
@61   = ~So I 'ave a chance after all. Ha! ha!~
@62   = ~Girly I admire yer passion when it comes to fightin'! ye have an unquenchable bloodlust like meself once battle is engaged.~
@63   = ~You admire my work? A bloody battlefield is an art form in its own right. The aftermath is one as well, especially if there are prisoners.~
@64   = ~Prisoners eh?~
@65   = ~Oh yes, yes! Prisoners make for a useful tool to send a message to any surrounding villages and homesteads.~
@66   = ~Lining the roads with crucified prisoners or severed heads on pikes always sent a message. My message to them was to surrender to my army or become like those who would dare oppose us.~
@67   = ~Aye sounds like me clan. Ye should 'ave been born a dwarf and we could 'ave been kin folk!~
@68   = ~Uh yeah, sounds interesting Korgan. I think <CHARNAME> wants us to get going, how time goes by quickly.~
@69   = ~Anomen, are you a knight, a real for goodness knight yet?~
@70   = ~I am a squire who is working to be in the Order. I have spent most of my life dedicated to the Order and becoming a knight would be a great honor.~
@71   = ~What will you do if you fail to get into the Order? Only those who are good enough, or have good influence are able to get accepted. So I heard.~
@72   = ~Are you implying that I am not good enough to be accepted? I am sure I am good enough to become a Knight of the Order.~
@73   = ~Well tin head you are on the right track with that arrogant thinking. You will fit in nicely.~
@74   = ~Bah! What would a common ruffian know about the Order. Leave me, this conversation is over!~
@75   = ~Sorry, I didn't mean to hurt your ego.~
@76   = ~Hey there, Callisto, would you like a turnip?~
@77   = ~Turnip? What in the Nine Hells are you talking about little man?~
@78   = ~A turnip, you know food, food that tastes great. Turnips are well known for their benefits. They make your complexion look very nice, gives your hair that nice shiny glow, brightens your teeth to a nice shiny white.......~
@79   = ~Ohh would you shut up already!! I don't want any turnips nor do I care for their benefits!~
@80   = ~But there are so many benefits of eating turnips. Another benefit, which would help you out greatly, is they make you mellow and less aggressive. Turnips will zap that aggression and make you a friendly person in the long run.~
@81   = ~Arrgghh! Someone make it stop! Keep waging that tongue and I will cut it out!~
@82   = ~If you did that, then I would not be able to taste my turnip surprise pie. Mmmmm very tasty it is!~
@83   = ~I give up! Give me one of those turnips if it will shut you up!~
@84   = ~See I knew you would change your mind. Here my friend enjoy!~
@85   = ~Turnip for your thoughts?~
@86   = ~Oh do go away gnome!~
@87   = ~Come now, Callisto, why don't you like me? I'm easy to get along with. I give you turnips for free when I could make a fortune off them. But no I give them away as a gift to you.~
@88   = ~You are the most annoying little man I've met!~
@89   = ~Annoying, my child? Why of course not. I'm just a friendly gnome trying to make his way in the world, providing a service to some and bring a smile to others.~
@90   = ~I have no desire...~
@91   = ~Why of course we all have desires. That's what Great Uncle Rupert used to say. Well that is until his tongue was ripped out and then he couldn't speak well any more.~
@92   = ~By the gods when...~
@93   = ~The gods? No they didn't help poor Great Uncle Rupert. No divine intervention for him.~
@94   = ~Quiet fool!! One more word and I swear I'll scream!~
@95   = ~But...~
@96   = ~ARGHHHH!!~ [cmca11]
@97   = ~Aerie, Aerie, you're such a young, innocent, wide-eyed elf, I just find it...refreshing!~
@98   = ~W-why do you say that?~
@99   = ~I say that dear little one because such a trait makes you an easy target for someone to corrupt.~
@100  = ~I-I am starting to dislike you. You're evil. J-just leave me alone!~
@101  = ~Oh Aerie, Aerie, Aerie what fun would that be if I left you alone? What is evil any way? You may be innocent and "good" but deep down you want to tear the people apart who were responsible for hacking your wings off don't you? You want them to suffer for what they did to you.~
@102  = ~I-I am not like you! I will not ever let hate control me like it has done to you. Your soul has been eaten away because you let hate and revenge control your life! I heard about you from stories in the circus. You use to have an army that went around and destroyed villages and killed people all because someone did the same thing to you in your childhood and...~
@103  = ~(Callisto glares at Aerie.) You, my dear are treading in dangerous waters. I admire your sudden backbone by speaking your mind to someone like me, but mention my past again and I guarantee you will know what pain is!~
@104  = ~L-leave me alone!~
@105  = ~(Callisto smiles at Aerie.) Nice chatting, Aerie.~
@106  = ~Oh my! Looky here, the wingless wonder is injured! Does it hurt much, are you in pain? Poor, poor baby!~
@107  = ~L-leave me alone y-you wretch!~
@108  = ~Leave you alone? I am simply concerned with your welfare my dear. Is it wrong to look out for my fellow elf?~
@109  = ~I d-doubt you have my welfare in mind. A-all you care about is yourself!~
@110  = ~Come now my little peach even I can show compassion to others, believe it or not.~
@111  = ~Compassion? I am surprised you even know the word. You're evil and compassion is beyond the grasp of those who are evil.~
@112  = ~Your outlook on "good" and "evil" is pretty black and white wingless elf. You're a young short sighted fool, Aerie, my little pet. In time you will know the meaning of true evil.~
@113  = ~W-why do you keep looking at me?~
@114  = ~Do I make you nervous wingless wonder? Do I inspire fear and terror that sends coldness down your spine?~
@115  = ~The only thing you conjure up in me, is revulsion.~
@116  = ~Well at least I have an effect on you, Aerie, my little sweet.~
@117  = ~Jaheira, why do you keep looking at me? See anything you desire?~
@118  = ~I certainly do not! I was thinking about taking you to the Harpers. You're a wanted criminal after all.~
@119  = ~It's so good to feel wanted and needed!~
@120  = ~This is not a trivial matter to make fun of! Maybe it would serve you right if I did bring you in.~
@121  = ~Well Miss High and Mighty why not bring me in? Is it because <CHARNAME> would not allow it, hmmm?~
@122  = ~As a matter of fact it does. <PRO_HESHE> knows what's good for this group and I will go along with it. But in my opinion your being here is wrong.~
@123  = ~Well it seems you contradict your own beliefs. By doing what <CHARNAME> wishes you go against your beliefs as a Harper.~
@124  = ~Enough already! What do you know of Harper rules? What do you know of me? Nothing! Drop the subject, Callisto.~
@125  = ~Why yes I shall drop it for now. The queen is getting all flustered at the moment.~
@126  = ~Jaheira, I have a question for you, well more of an inquiry actually.~
@127  = ~Ask if you wish Callisto.~
@128  = ~Rumor has it you were married at one time?~
@129  = ~Yes I was, his name was Khalid. He d-died while we were held captive.~
@130  = ~Ah I see.~
@131  = ~Is there anything else?~
@132  = ~Now that you mention it yes. I heard he was a cowardly little man that lacked a backbone. True?~
@133  = ~W-what? How dare you! I'd strike you down where you stand if it was not for <CHARNAME>! Never speak of Khalid again or I may forget your value in this group.~
@134  = ~Opps! Sorry. I did not know it was a touchy subject.~
@135  = ~I am curious as to why you didn't get yourself out of that dungeon.~
@136  = ~What do you mean? My weapons and armor were taken from me and the jail door was locked.~
@137  = ~Well I thought that since you are a halfling, you could pick the lock and free yourself.~
@138  = ~(Mazzy looks at Callisto dumbfounded.)~
@139  = ~Well?~
@140  = ~You have a narrow, racist mind, Callisto. Not all halflings are thieves, pick pockets and lock pickers. I will have you know that I am a knight, a warrior for good.~
@141  = ~Aww! I find that cute in an amusing way. A little runt fighter!~
@142  = ~Perhaps a demonstration of my abilities will alter your thinking? I will not stand by and be rediculed by the likes of you.~
@143  = ~No that will not be necessary pumpkin. I'll take your word for it. I should not have pushed you, knowing that halflings have a *short* temper.~
@144  = ~Why do you keep on antagonizing the members in our adventuring group? Are you truly that much of a sadist?~
@145  = ~Hmm?~
@146  = ~What do you mean?~
@147  = ~I mean you are antagonistic, confrontational with everyone including myself. I find it unnecessarily childish. Borish actually.~
@148  = ~Mazzy, Mazzy, I am afraid you misunderstand me. I am brightening an otherwise boring day, plus it keeps everyone on their toes, keeping them focused on the task at hand.~
@149  = ~I fail to understand your reasoning in this. I hardly consider it brightening one's day and how does it keep us focused?~
@150  = ~Must I play connect the dots? Show you how point A connects to point B to point C? What a bore!~
@151  = ~Oh very well. With my playfulness, my confrontation self, it keeps you tense and not relaxed. By staying tense you will not be caught off guard or surprised by a possible opponent. Simple really.~
@152  = ~I find your line of reasoning shall I say, crazy.~
@153  = ~Crazy you say? Perhaps so my little pumpkin, perhaps so.~
@154  = ~Minsc! Keep that filthy rodent away from me. It crawls on me begging for food whenever we stop to eat. I am starting to get annoyed with it and those that annoy me, meet an unfortunate fate.~
@155  = ~Boo must like your food. I don't know why he goes to you, what I have is good for him.~
@156  = ~Could it be that your rodent doesn't like mold on the bread? You really need to keep your supplies of food in better condition after all.~
@157  = ~But Minsc thinks the bread taste better with a little bit of mold on it. It gives it a special flavor!~
@158  = ~(Callisto looks at Minsc and walks away.)~
@159  = ~You don't like moldy bread, Callisto? Callisto? Ah well more moldy bread for Minsc and Boo!~
@160  = ~Minsc is amazed at your ferocity in battle! You fight like a Rashaman warrior in a berserker frenzy!~
@161  = ~At a young age I had a fire lit in me that has burned with me since then. It burns brightly when I fight, keeps me focused on my enemy until their blood soaks up the battlefield. The fire in me is rage, rage that will forever burn until I die.~
@162  = ~Rage is good! It keeps you fighting, fighting hard so you don't notice aches and pains from swinging the sword nor getting hit. I have been hit on the head many times during battle and never noticed it until the fight is over. Massive headache sets in, oww!!~
@163  = ~Really? I was always wondered what happened to you, now I know, too many blows to the head.~
@164  = ~Well mother was always clumsy when I was a babe and sometimes dropped me on my head! But that is all good! It has made Minsc a great able fighter!~
@165  = ~A decent fighter you may be, but not very intelligent.~
@166  = ~Well Boo has the brains and Minsc has the brawn. A good working team we are! Butt kicking for goodness!~
@167  = ~I give up trying to hold a conversation with you.~
@168  = ~Nalia, my dear, why do you journey with <CHARNAME>? One of noble blood may get her hands dirty during our grand adventures.~
@169  = ~I travel with <CHARNAME> in order to help those who are in need. Also, with helping the needy, people may change their impressions about nobles.~
@170  = ~Wow! Our very own bleeding heart in our merry little group! Wonderful!~
@171  = ~I'm surprised you would get your pretty soft hands soiled in being an adventurer.~
@172  = ~I am nothing like your typical nobles. I gladly help those in need and if I happen to get my hands dirty from it, so be it.~
@173  = ~I am touched, truly I am. Well not really. I would prefer to stick my sword in your heart and watch it bleed. Then you would truly be a bleeding heart.~
@174  = ~I find your fighting skills very worthy of a warrior. A shame that it's wasted on being paladin for goodness.~
@175  = ~My skills of a warrior, a paladin, are not wasted on helping those out for the greater good.~
@176  = ~The greater good... (Callisto pauses to think before she continues.)~
@177  = ~Where were these do-gooders when my village was attacked and razed to the ground? Where hundreds lost their lives to the evilness of the drow and their lap dogs?~
@178  = ~Cal-~
@179  = ~I will tell you where they were, sitting in their lofty, safe positions in the city, that's where they were at! People like you preach about helping others but when it comes to action, they do nothing!~
@180  = ~I am sorry for your loss, but those who attacked your village are at fault. I am confused about...~
@181  = ~It's nothing, never mind! I no longer wish to talk about this!~
@182  = ~I notice when you are engaged in combat, you fight with reckless abandonment and a habit of taking no quarter.~
@183  = ~Oh that I do! Once the battle is engaged, my bloodlust takes over and bodies begin to pile up around me.~
@184  = ~Such intensity can lead you open for an attack or it may endanger fellow comrades. Your fighting style reminds me of a dwarven battlerager going berserk in the heat of battle.~
@185  = ~I have heard of dwarven battleragers, they are a force to be recon with. My style is of my own and far more deadly compared to them. If I get hit, no proble. If I die, like I really care.~
@186  = ~If collateral damage occurs, no problem. They should not have gotten in my way to begin with.~
@187  = ~I find your attitude troubling and I will be watching you, watching you carefully.~
@188  = ~Watch me? I'm suppose to care that you're watching me? Ha! Kill 'em all!~
@189  = ~You do that on someone who is for good and righteousness, I'll end you.~
@190  = ~Such a pretty day for a blood bath, don't you think?~ [cmca36]
@191  = ~We are in the beautiful outdoors, watching the greatness of nature and all you can think about is death?~
@192  = ~Why yes my little tree hugger. Watching the forest become engulfed in flames with the black smoke darkening the blue sky, it is a beautiful, just a beautiful scene!~
@193  = ~Truly you do not mean that. You are of the elven folk, those who are in touch with nature, you should love, nurture nature, not be a destroyer of it.~
@194  = ~So? What does having elven blood have anything to do with being a protector of nature? Ah yes, a typical stereotype from you humans.~
@195  = ~I am sorry, you are correct. Drow elves, for the most part, have no respect for nature either. *Not* that I am not making any comparisons mind you.~
@196  = ~(At the mere mention of the word drow, a flash of rage shows on Callisto's face.)~
@197  = ~(Cernd lets the conversation drop, thus leaving Callisto to ponder on what was said.)~
@198  = ~You are the first tiefling I have ever met, Haer'Dalis. And I am curious about something.~
@199  = ~About what?~
@200  = ~Have you heard of my adventures in carnage?~
@201  = ~Nay, can't say that I have.~
@202  = ~You haven't? How disappointing. I thought my conquering exploits were well known.~
@203  = ~I am afraid my dear falcon that your ego out shines your "exploits".~
@204  = ~Now that is amusing, a pansy bard calling me ego centric. Ha! Ha!~
@205  = ~My dear falcon, I am curious about something.~
@206  = ~Oh? What would that be my fleety little man?~
@207  = ~There is so much rage in you, I wonder where it all comes from.~
@208  = ~What a wonderful question! Maybe my rage comes from being annoyed by pestering fools with nosey questions.~
@209  = ~The falcon is a wonderful actor who's life began in tragedy and in tragedy, the life will end.~
@210  = ~I can tell you a tragedy that is about ready to happen if the fleety little man keeps pushing it.~
@211  = ~Well since you...~
@212  = ~The rage that is burning inside me has been there since the day my village was laid waste and my family was killed!! Dead, dead, everyone was killed that day but me!~
@213  = ~Those filthy drow and those traitors! THE RAGE IN ME WILL BURN UNTIL THEY ARE ALL DEAD!! All of them dead... (Callisto stares off into the distance, saying nothing more.)~
@214  = ~Edwin, could you teach me some spell casting? I would love to learn some spells.~
@215  = ~Really? (As if your small mind could understand learning spells.) Let my greatness instruct you in the finer arts of magic? Looting and pillaging is not enough for you?~
@216  = ~I do so enjoy any advantage I can gain over an enemy. There are certain types of spells I would like to learn Edwin.~
@217  = ~What spells would they be?~
@218  = ~Fire based spells of course! Fireball, Agannazar Scorcher, Flame Arrow, and any others you could teach me.~
@219  = ~I see you have a fascination with fire.~
@220  = ~Oh yes I truly do, it's been a part of me since my childhood. So when do I get to learn this?~
@221  = ~I will have to think upon this for now. (How a simpleton could ever learn those spells is beyond me.)~
@222  = ~Heh. Ha! Ha! Ha!~
@223  = ~Is there something that you find amusing? Do indulge me.~
@224  = ~Why you, Eddy! You prance around the group claiming to be this great mage, yet you get fooled into reading that scroll. Now look at you. Truly amusing if you ask me.~
@225  = ~(I certainly did not ask you.) Why don't you go amuse yourself by pulling the wings off insects. That sort of pass time would suite you quite nicely.~
@226  = ~Watching your discomfort from your change is far more amusing, Eddy! The next time we are at a shop, you will have to purchase a pink robe.~
@227  = ~I should use a transformation spell on you, turning you into a mouse in a room full of cats. Now that would be amusing.~
@228  = ~Oh, Eddy, you're blushing. There's no reason to be embarrassed about this, laugh it off, have fun with it. Ha!.~
@229  = ~(Callisto's expression quickly turns serious.) Any more stupid threats like that and I may cut you open to see if your blood matches the redness of your blushing.~
@230  = ~Rest assured that none of my threats are stupid. If I was to act upon them, you would not know what hit you.~
@231  = ~You're a ranger aye? A protector of the great forests and hero of furry bunny rabbits? I find that so noble of you!~
@232  = ~Yes I am a ranger, a protector of the forests as you say. Why do you ask?~
@233  = ~Well, I heard rangers talk to animals and these animals talk back. Is this true?~
@234  = ~In my experience it is not true. I never had an animal communicate with me.~
@235  = ~What a shame! I was wondering what language they may talk back to you with. Would it be common or their own language I wonder?~
@236  = ~*Sigh* I will not hear any more of this foolishness. Go amuse yourself with someone else.~
@237  = ~Valygar, why do you look so glum today? Someone chop down your favorite tree?~
@238  = ~I am not in the mood for your nonsense.~
@239  = ~I can see you are not in the mood, which is why I asked the question.~
@240  = ~Are you always so annoying? Alright, fine, I'll tell you if it shut you up.~
@241  = ~I didn't sleep well last night if you must know. A lack of sleep always puts me in a foul mood. Callisto? Callisto?~
@242  = ~Huh?~
@243  = ~Did you hear a word I said?~
@244  = ~No, I was thinking about sharpening my dagger. It has been a while since I sharpen it last.~
@245  = ~(Valygar looks at Callisto with disgust, then walks away.)~
@246  = ~What's wrong? My dagger does need to be sharpen.~
@247  = ~Notice anything interesting, Yoshimo?~
@248  = ~You keep gawking at me. You must know about the bounty on my head.~
@249  = ~Why would I know about a bounty on you?~
@250  = ~You're a bounty hunter, it's your profession.~
@251  = ~Oh don't look at me like that. I heard some things about you and one of them is you're a bounty hunter from Kara-Tur.~
@252  = ~Ah, you have discovered my darkest secret.~
@253  = ~I wouldn't even think of trying to collect a reward on me. I would slice you in half without a second thought. Remember that.~
@254  = ~That is a nice looking blade you have there. I heard that Kara-Tur blades are well made, is this true?~
@255  = ~Yes, that is quite true. The katana is a perfect weapon made by the most talented craftsmen. It is light weight for speed, very durable and holds its edge for a long time before being sharpen.~
@256  = ~They're this good without being enchanted?~
@257  = ~Having an enchantment placed on them makes them better. They are a superior weapon compared to a longsword even if it is enchanted. I prefer a katana any day over any other blade.~
@258  = ~I may have to get myself one of these katanas. I will have to pay a visit to Kara-Tur and see about getting one of these.~
@259  = ~Be prepared to bring a lot of coin. Katanas are very expensive weapons.~
@260  = ~Coin is no problem. I will make them an offer that would be in their best interest not to refuse.~
@261  = ~Hey little bard I wrote a poem that you should hear.~
@262  = ~Really? *You* wrote a poem? Let me hear it.~
@263  = ~I knew a wingless wonder who could not fly.~
@264  = ~Many people asked and wondered why.~
@265  = ~She had no wings and that's no lie.~
@266  = ~On many nights she would cry.~
@267  = ~The wingless wonder wished she could die.~
@268  = ~Y-you're sick! I hate you!~
@269  = ~My little viper that was not nice, not at all. I think I shall write a sad tale about an elf with no soul.~
@270  = ~Hey I like that already! Make sure I get royalties when you have it published.~
@271  = ~C-come on, Haer 'dalis, leave her alone. She's just an attention seeker and a sick one at that.~
@272  = ~Fly, wingless wonder, fly!~
@273  = ~Hey Korgan, why don't we get Boo from Minsc and then we can play kick the hamster.~
@274  = ~Sounds like a grand idea to me!~
@275  = ~Boo, hide behind me! I shall protect you! You two will not touch a single hair on Boo. Righteous butt kicking will be handed out if you do!~
@276  = ~Minsc we are bored, we need something exciting to do.~
@277  = ~That rodent kin do somethin' useful fer once. All it does is eat our food.~
@278  = ~Argh! The first one that approaches me will be tossed all the way to Baldur's Gate!~
@279  = ~Calm down my large dim witted friend, we were joking. Come on. Korgan, we can go smash up a tavern instead.~
@280  = ~Ninafer, my dear, you fit the persona of a Gold Elf perfectly. You're stuck up, judgemental, full of yourself and think you are better than anyone else.~
@281  = ~Really? Are you not a Gold Elf yourself?~
@282  = ~That I am, but I'm nothing like our kind, no, not at all.~
@283  = ~I agree with you on that. Your typical Gold Elf is not a sadistic, homicidal maniac ready to see the world burn because life was unfair to her.~
@284  = ~See, there you go with your holier than thou attitude. I have a few flaws and you speak to me as if I was beneath you.~
@285  = ~(Nina rolls her eyes and says nothing more.)~
@286  = ~Are homocidal urges all that drive you, Callisto? Your give no quarter approach in battle is baffling.~
@287  = ~Baffling? Why should I allow an enemy to live so they can fight me another day? Better to butcher them now and be done with it.~
@288  = ~Have you ever heard of the word redemption? They may see that their evil ways is wrong and may wish to atone for their crimes.~
@289  = ~(Callisto looks at Ninafer dumbfounded.)~
@290  = ~Was there something I said that you do not understand?~
@291  = ~Redemption is for the weak and so is showing mercy to your enemy. We're from two different worlds sister. You stick with your flawed perception of reality and I'll stick with mine.~
@292  = ~So be it, *sister*.~
@293  = ~I heard you lost your parents at a young age, Ninafer. It would seem we have something in common after all.~
@294  = ~Yes I did. Not only did I lose my parents but I also lost both of my sisters. That part of my past I know very little about though. My adoptive father has said little about it, he either does not know or is unwilling to tell me. I never really pressed the matter with him to tell you the truth.~
@295  = ~You lost both sisters? I lost both of my sisters and the rest of my family when the invaders razed my village. One was decapitated before my eyes and the other, the baby, I never saw again.~
@296  = ~I do not recall my family, I was a baby at the time it happen.~
@297  = ~(Nina studies Callisto for a long moment.) D-do you think, could it be...~
@298  = ~(Callisto explodes in a rage.) No! Don't say it! It can't be! This is nothing but a strange coincidence that is all!~
@299  = ~But what if...~
@300  = ~Shut up! Enough! I won't hear this! This conversation is over, leave me! Don't ever speak to me again!~
@301  = ~(Callisto storms off. A tear starts to trickle down the side of her face which she wipes off fiercely. She regains control of her emotions, the cold unemotional look returns to her face.) My family is dead.~
